paragraph.math:
$$\begin{array}{lll}
      m & = & {f\left( \mathbf{v}\prime\text{)} = f\left( c_{1}\mathbf{v}_{1} + \cdots + c_{k}\mathbf{v}_{k} \right) \right.} \\
       & = & {c_{1}f\left( \mathbf{v}_{1} \right) + \cdots + c_{k}f\left( \mathbf{v}_{k} \right)} \\
       & < & {c_{1}m + \cdots + c_{k}m = m\left( c_{1} + \cdots + c_{k} \right) = m}
      \end{array}$$

example.paragraph:
Given points $\textbf{p}_{1} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      0
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ $\textbf{p}_{2} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      3 \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ and $\textbf{p}_{3} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      1 \\
      2
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$ in ${\mathbb{R}}^{2}\text{,}$ let $S = \text{conv}\{\textbf{p}_{1},\textbf{p}_{2},\textbf{p}_{3}\}\text{.}$ For each linear functional $f\text{,}$ find the maximum value $m$ of $f$ on the set $S\text{,}$ and find all points $\textbf{x}$ in $S$ at which $f(\textbf{x}) = m\text{.}$

statement.paragraph:
Given points $\textbf{p}_{1} = \begin{bmatrix}
      1 \\
      0
      \end{bmatrix}$, $\textbf{p}_{2} = \begin{bmatrix}
      2 \\
      3
      \end{bmatrix}$, and $\textbf{p}_{3} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      2
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$ in $\text{ℝ}^{2}$, let $S = \text{conv}\left\{ \textbf{p}_{1},\textbf{p}_{2},\textbf{p}_{3} \right\}$. For each linear functional $f$, find the maximum value $m$ of $f$ on the set $S$, and find all points $\textbf{x}$ in $S$ at which $f\left( \textbf{x} \right) = m$.﻿

